<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <title>Programming Languages | <%= title %></title>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
    </head>

    <body>
        <%- include('partials/header') %>
        <main>
        <figure>
            <img src="/img/pls.png" alt="Image of Programming Languages">

            <figcaption>
                <a href="https://careerkarma.com/blog/how-many-coding-languages-are-there/">
                    There are over 50 widely used programming languages.
                </a>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section>
            <h2>Introduction</h2>

            <p>
                A programming language is a way to express instructions that a
                computer can execute. Programmers use languages to create software
                including websites, mobile applications, games, and operating systems.
            </p>

            <p>
                Different programming languages provide different rules for how
                instructions are written, data is organized, and programs function.
                Each language has its own strengths and weaknesses depending on
                the purpose.
            </p>

            <p>
                This website introduces four widely used programming languages:
                Python, JavaScript, Java, and C++.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="language-columns">

            <div>
                <h2>Python</h2>
                <p>
                    Python is known for its readable syntax and is commonly used
                    for automation, data analysis, and artificial intelligence.
                </p>
                <a href="/python">Learn More</a>
            </div>

            <div>
                <h2>JavaScript</h2>
                <p>
                    JavaScript is used to create interactive websites and
                    develop both frontend and backend applications.
                </p>
                <a href="/javascript">Learn More</a>
            </div>

            <div>
                <h2>Java</h2>
                <p>
                    Java is an object-oriented programming language commonly
                    used for enterprise software and application development.
                </p>
                <a href="/java">Learn More</a>
            </div>

            <div>
                <h2>C++</h2>
                <p>
                    C++ is known for its performance and is commonly used
                    for game development, operating systems, and other
                    high-performance applications.
                </p>
                <a href="/cpp">Learn More</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="tech-phrase">
            <h2>Random Phrase</h2>

            <p><%= techPhrase %></p>

            <p class="note">
                Data from the <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@faker-js/faker">Faker Node.js package</a>.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
    </body>
</html>